# F1 (docs/monorepo-boundaries.md, "A port translates: the foreign boundary").
# Every source file that waits on an API this codebase does not own (a native
# plugin, `navigator`, `Notification`) outside `callForeign` from
# `@some-ui/intent-kit`, with exactly how many such waits it has (`await`,
# `for await`, `.then`/`.catch`/`.finally`). `pnpm check:foreign-boundary`
# fails on any file missing here, and on any count that no longer matches, in
# either direction.
#
# One entry per line: `<sites> <path>`. A blank line ends a group, and each
# group's `#` lines must include one starting `Unbounded:` (why this wait needs
# no deadline, no classified failure and no report) or `Grandfathered:`. A new
# entry, or a raised count, goes in its own group under `Unbounded:`; it never
# joins or raises the grandfathered group. The usual answer is not an entry at
# all: run the wait through `callForeign`, and the count goes away.
#
# This file is where F1 is reviewed. The check counts; it does not judge.

# Grandfathered: these waited on a foreign API before F1 landed. Debt, not a
# judgment that each is fine: apps/www/src/lib/dictation is the one #1671's
# notes shipped broken on (a recognizer that cannot start reads as a frame of
# "Listening…" and a notice that blames the speaker). A count here may only
# fall (lower it in the same change), and an entry leaves when its file stops
# waiting outside the boundary.
11 apps/www/src/lib/device-backend/capacitor-sqlite/index.ts
1 apps/www/src/lib/device-backend/native-http/index.ts
1 apps/www/src/lib/device-backend/storage/index.ts
6 apps/www/src/lib/device-speech/native.ts
4 apps/www/src/lib/dictation/index.ts
